index e6524e0..ebc74c7 100644
--- a/Design_Docs/GARUDA-AHB2APB-SPEC-001.md
+++ b/Design_Docs/GARUDA-AHB2APB-SPEC-001.md
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 |---|---|---|
 | 1.0–1.4 | Bridge with `pclk` generated by an ICG at 125 MHz, claimed 50% duty and "no CDC" | — |
 | 2.0 | `pclk` generation moves to `clk_div` as a toggle flop (an ICG cannot produce 50% duty). The no-CDC claim is replaced with a proof. Per-window `APB_DIV`. Window map regenerated from `GARUDA-SYS-001` after the peripheral reassignment. | ADR-0002, 0008, 0020 |
+| 2.0a | [N-7.20] states the single `PSLVERR` rule: only for an offset that is not a register; a write to a read-only register is ignored (Track A task 0.5, 2026-10-12). | AUD-13 |
 
 ## 0.3 Normative references
 
@@ -335,8 +336,12 @@ fault as fatal and reset.
 ### 7.7 SLVERR
 
 **[N-7.20]** A window asserting `PSLVERR` with `PREADY` causes the bridge to return a
-two-cycle AHB ERROR. Peripherals assert `PSLVERR` for unmapped offsets within their own
-window and for illegal field writes, as defined in each peripheral's own specification.
+two-cycle AHB ERROR. One rule holds for every peripheral (AUD-13, ruled 2026-10-11 in the
+two-track plan): `PSLVERR` is raised only for an offset that is not a register in the
+window; a write to a read-only register is ignored and raises no error. *(Until 2026-10-12
+this note left the choice to each peripheral's specification, and the timers and the DMA
+answered `PSLVERR` to a read-only write while the CLIC, the reset controller and the shim
+ignored it.)*
 
 **[N-7.21]** All three error sources — sub-word, unmapped window, `PSLVERR` — produce the
 identical AHB two-cycle ERROR. The master cannot distinguish them, and does not need to:
