 **[N-6.4]** Channel 4 serves the SPI slave (ESP32 / ESP-NOW mesh), **restored and required
 per ADR-0020 Rev 2** (APF's neighbour-position source). Its registers, interrupts and
-arbiter position already exist and work; `dma_req_i[4]` is still tied low at the top level
-and **must be un-tied when `rtl/spi_slave/` is built** (RTL work item). Pending that, CH4
-carries no traffic. The final pin outcome is gated on OPEN-2 (ADR-0020 Rev 2).
+arbiter position already exist and work, and `rtl/spi_slave/` is built with its request
+wired to `dma_req_i[4]` (`garuda_chip_top.v`), so CH4 carries traffic. *(Updated 2026-10-12:
+the text said the line was still tied low.)* The final pin outcome is gated on OPEN-2
+(ADR-0020 Rev 2).
 
 **[N-6.5]** The priority order is by consequence of not being serviced. The IMU is the
 control loop's hard-real-time input and is highest. The console is lowest because nothing
 depends on it — dropping a debug character is free. GPS at 115200 baud is one beat every
 ~21,700 `hclk` cycles, so its low priority costs nothing.
 
+### 6.4 Register-port errors
+
+**[N-6.6]** `PSLVERR` is raised only for an offset that is not a register: channels 6 and 7
+(`0xC0`–`0xFC`), `+0x18` and `+0x1C` in each channel, `0x104` and above, and unaligned
+offsets. A write to a read-only register (`STAT`, `GSTAT`) is ignored and raises no error;
+`ICLR` reads 0. This is the single rule of `GARUDA-AHB2APB-SPEC-001` [N-7.20] (AUD-13, ruled
+in the two-track plan, 2026-10-11). Until 2026-10-12 the DMA answered `PSLVERR` to a write
+to `STAT` or `GSTAT`.
